        "title": "Section 1-2 \u2014 Notices & Recruitment Procedures",
        "body": "Section 1: Workplace Notices\n\nNotice A: Staff Cafeteria — Hot meals served 11:30am - 2:00pm Monday through Friday. Cold sandwiches, salads, and barista coffee available 7:30am - 4:00pm. Weekends closed, so the cafeteria is not open on Saturday morning. The evening kiosk closes at 4:00pm sharp.\n\nNotice B: Quarterly Health & Safety Evacuation Drill — Scheduled for Thursday at 10:30am. All personnel must proceed via designated fire stairwells to Assembly Point C in the North Car Park, situated in the North Car Park beside the visitor bays. Under no circumstances may passenger lifts be operated during the drill, even when carrying heavy loads. Marshals will sweep each floor; staff should not delay to collect belongings.\n\nNotice C: Company Information Center & Learning Commons — Standard book and digital device loans are 3 weeks in duration. Overdue penalties are 50p per business day. Materials may be renewed online up to twice, a maximum of two renewals, provided no other staff member has placed a reservation. There is no emergency delivery service to remote offices mentioned in this notice; reservations are collected from the front desk only.\n\nSection 2: Professional Development & Recruitment\nCompany policy outlines a standardized three-tier recruitment procedure divided into three standardized tiers. Stage 1 consists of a 20-minute telephonic HR screening interview conducted by Human Resources (HR); the initial screening call lasts approximately 20 minutes. Stage 2 entails a technical skills evaluation assessing candidate technical skills through work-sample tasks. Stage 3 is a comprehensive panel review featuring the department head and external client liaison; the panel includes an external client liaison alongside the hiring manager. Formal outcome documentation and constructive feedback, written feedback described as constructive in nature, are transmitted to all applicants — not only successful ones — within 5 business days. Interviews are held on site; virtual attendance upon request and automatic second-chance interviews for missed appointments are not offered under current policy.\n\nSection 3: Training & Feedback\nMonthly workshops run 2:00pm - 3:30pm in Room 4B. Attendance is recorded; slides are posted within 24 hours. Probation reviews occur at week 6 and week 12 with written constructive notes. As with recruitment, every applicant and trainee receives formal outcome documentation within 5 business days of assessment."
